! Hirshfeld atom refinement of quartz using nearest-neighbour atom-centred
! fragments at level 0 with hydrogen capping -- the L0+H model of Davidson
! (2023) chapter 5. RHF/def2-SVP. About 7 s.
!
! Level 0 means each fragment is a single asymmetric unit atom with every
! bond replaced by a capping hydrogen: silane around the silicon and water
! around the oxygen. It is the degenerate case of the scheme and, as the
! thesis reports, a poor model of quartz -- which is exactly why it is worth
! testing. Its value here is as the LOW anchor for the level-1 job: GoF^2
! collapses from 77.4 at level 0 to 9.8 at level 1, a factor of 8.
!
! AGREEMENT WITH THE THESIS, measured 2026-08-15, HF/def2-SVP L0 column:
!
!                        this job      thesis
!    R(F) / R1           0.0213        0.0306
!    GoF^2               77.367        103.02
!    r(Si-O) /A          1.61(4)       1.611(15)
!    U_iso(Si) /A^2      0.003(4)      0.0028(14)
!    U_iso(O)  /A^2      0.00564(10)   0.00575(11)
!
! Structure and GoF^2 agree to the precision either can claim. R(F) is the
! weakest agreement of any figure in either quartz job -- 30% apart, against
! 5-7% at level 1 -- and is NOT fully accounted for by the different data
! reduction (1009 reflections here, 1134 in the thesis). Unexplained; noted
! rather than blessed away. Level 0 is the pathological model, so it may be
! nothing, but if this reference is ever re-blessed, check it.
!
! See tests/long/quartz_NN_HAR_L1_rhf_def2-SVP/IO for the special-position
! standard-uncertainty problem, which is larger here: the silicon position su
! is 0.05 A against the oxygen's 0.0004 A.
!
! Known output defects, present in this reference and NOT to be blessed away:
! Rw(F2) prints NaN, R_sigma(F2) prints 0.0000, and every reflection is
! reported as an unmatched Friedel pair.

   input:   quartz_init.cif
   input:   HKLdata.quartz
